# Cairo / Starknet build artifacts. Each case's clean/ and planted/
# directory is a full Scarb project; running `scarb build` and
# `snforge test` locally produces target/ and .snfoundry_cache/ under
# the case dir. NEVER commit these — CI rebuilds from source on every
# push, and committed artifacts decay against the pinned toolchain.
**/target/
**/target/dev/
**/target/release/
**/target/CACHEDIR.TAG
**/.snfoundry_cache/

# Scarb lockfile. Not committed in the cf-invariants references and
# kept off-tree here for the same reason — the pinned scarb / snforge
# versions in each case's Scarb.toml are the reproducibility surface,
# and a stale Scarb.lock fights the pinned toolchain on dep refresh.
**/Scarb.lock

# EVM (Foundry) build artifacts. Each case's clean/ and planted/ is a full
# Foundry project; running `forge build` and `forge test` locally produces
# out/, cache/, and (via `forge install`) lib/ under the case dir. NEVER
# commit these — CI re-installs forge-std + rebuilds from source on every
# push, and committed artifacts decay against the pinned toolchain.
**/out/
**/cache/
**/lib/
**/broadcast/

# Case 8 vendors Guardian's EthenaTimelockController.sol under the case's
# lib/ tree because Guardian's `EthenaTimelockDefender` repo is not a
# Foundry package (no foundry.toml / no `forge install`-ready layout).
# The vendored source, its LICENSE, and its NOTICE must ship in-tree so
# fresh-clone CI compiles. Un-ignore that specific sub-path, then
# explicitly re-ignore the `forge install --no-git` install targets so
# they never sneak into a commit under case 8's lib/.
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/clean/lib/
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/clean/lib/ethena-timelock-defender/
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/clean/lib/ethena-timelock-defender/**
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/planted/lib/
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/planted/lib/ethena-timelock-defender/
!cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/planted/lib/ethena-timelock-defender/**
cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/clean/lib/forge-std/
cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/clean/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/
cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/planted/lib/forge-std/
cases/08-evm-ethena-timelock-selector/planted/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/

# Top-level `lib/` holds reviewer-reference submodules (Guardian's
# EthenaTimelockDefender @ main, OpenZeppelin contracts v5.x). Submodule
# gitlinks are tracked via .gitmodules regardless, but un-ignoring the
# path keeps `git status` clean and lets a `--recursive` clone populate
# the working tree without noise.
!/lib/
!/lib/**

# Move / Sui build artifacts. Each Move case's clean/ and planted/ is a
# full Sui Move package; running `sui move build` and `sui move test`
# locally produces build/ and Move.lock under the case dir. Same
# rationale — CI rebuilds from source on every push, and committed
# artifacts decay against the pinned sui CLI.
**/build/
**/Move.lock

# Solana / Anchor (Cargo) build artifacts. Each Solana case's clean/
# and planted/ is a Cargo workspace; running `cargo test` locally
# produces target/ and Cargo.lock under the case dir. NEVER commit
# these — CI rebuilds from source on every push, and committed
# artifacts decay against the pinned rustc / anchor-lang versions in
# the program Cargo.toml. proptest persists minimal-failing-input
# regression files alongside the test source; those are reproducible
# from the proptest seed and the source, so they stay off-tree.
**/Cargo.lock
**/*.proptest-regressions

# Secrets — same envelope as cf-invariants.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# OS junk.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
